<header class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow mint">/ terms</p><h1>Use thoughtfully.<br />Keep your judgment.</h1><p>Effective October 23, 2026. Updated November 18, 2026.</p></header><article class="prose info-content"><h2>Using GuideHollow</h2><p>GuideHollow provides original educational AI guides, structured prompt templates, downloadable practice datasets, and four client-side browser utilities. By reading pages or using any browser utility on this site, you agree to these terms. You may read articles, adapt prompt patterns for personal or workplace tasks, and download sample practice fixtures for verification exercises, while remaining solely responsible for verifying suitability and accuracy before acting on any output.</p><h2>Educational material and verification boundaries</h2><p>All articles, checklists, diagrams, and worked examples on GuideHollow are general educational material. Nothing on this site constitutes personalized legal, financial, medical, tax, compliance, or cybersecurity incident advice, nor does any guide guarantee how a third-party AI model or software product will respond in your environment. Software interfaces, context limits, sharing settings, and safety rules change frequently; always compare critical details against current official vendor documentation and qualified domain reviewers.</p><h2>Tools and your inputs</h2><p>Our four browser utilities serve distinct purposes: the Prompt Builder formats your instructions without calling an AI model; the Response Quality Checklist records your own review; the Weighted Average Audit Workbench computes an illustrative weighted price from supplied rows; and the Source Claim Verifier compares your choices with an editor-written answer key for fictional case notes and lets you assemble a separate human-reviewed source-claim ledger that you can download as TSV and later re-import locally to resume. Importing replaces current work only after validating the file and requesting confirmation when there are existing rows or unfinished input. The manual ledger does not verify claims automatically. Their outputs are not professional certification, independently verified real-world facts, live model benchmarks, or guarantees of any business outcome. All calculations and user selections happen in your browser; the claim verifier displays its published fictional source notes directly in the page and downloads the public answer-key CSV from this website.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Browser utility</th><th>Runs on your device</th><th>What it verifies</th><th>What stays your responsibility</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href="/tools/ai-prompt-builder/">AI Prompt Builder</a></td><td>Formats five fields into structured prompt text locally</td><td>Presence of goal field and draft-stale protection</td><td>Checking whether an external AI obeys your constraints</td></tr><tr><td><a href="/tools/ai-response-checklist/">Response Quality Checklist</a></td><td>Tracks completion across six review checkpoints</td><td>Visual progress of your self-review steps</td><td>Confirming actual citations, totals, dates, and safety</td></tr><tr><td><a href="/tools/weighted-price-checker/">Weighted Average Audit</a></td><td>Computes unit sum, revenue, and weighted mean in JavaScript</td><td>Row formatting, negative inputs, and arithmetic consistency</td><td>Authenticity and completeness of real business invoices</td></tr><tr><td><a href="/tools/claim-checker/">Source Claim Verifier</a></td><td>Scores practice cases and manages a local TSV claim ledger</td><td>Matches against built-in teaching keys and TSV schema checks</td><td>Independent verification of real-world documents you cite</td></tr></tbody></table><p>You retain full control over text you enter, copy, or export inside your browser. GuideHollow never sends tool form text to an external backend database or AI endpoint. Avoid typing confidential workplace records, passwords, API secrets, or personal data on shared computers, and check your browser's own downloads list before closing a tab after requesting a TXT or TSV export.</p><h2>Downloadable practice fixtures</h2><p>The CSV, TSV, TXT, PDF, and XLSX files hosted in our <a href="/evidence/">Evidence Library</a> are non-sensitive teaching datasets created specifically so readers can reproduce spreadsheet, OCR, Unicode, and claim-auditing lessons offline. Do not represent our sample transactions, sample meeting notes, or sample claims as live commercial sales figures or third-party AI benchmark scores.</p><h2>Availability and external links</h2><p>We strive to keep guides, calculators, feeds, and sample downloads reliable and fast, but we do not guarantee uninterrupted uptime or real-time synchronization with external software updates. External links to OpenAI, Google, Microsoft, Anthropic, W3C, or GitHub lead to third-party services governed by their own terms and privacy policies. Linking to documentation as a reference does not imply vendor endorsement or ongoing accuracy beyond the documented review date.</p><h2>Content and intellectual property</h2><p>GuideHollow's original articles, diagrams, tools, and branding are protected by applicable copyright and intellectual property laws. You are welcome to quote brief passages with attribution, link directly to guides, and adapt prompt templates for internal team workflows. Republishing complete articles verbatim, scraping tool pages to mirror the site, or presenting GuideHollow's name and diagrams as your own requires prior written permission. Public visibility of repository source files for verification does not grant an unrestricted commercial brand license.</p><h2>Acceptable use and security</h2><p>You may not interfere with site hosting, probe infrastructure with automated abuse traffic, inject misleading content into public links, or use this site to facilitate credential misuse or fraud. Public correction issues submitted through GitHub are governed by GitHub's terms and become publicly visible—never submit secrets or private third-party records there.</p><h2>Disclaimers, liability limits, and revisions</h2><p>To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, GuideHollow and all utilities are provided on an "as available" educational basis without implied warranties of merchantability, accuracy for every task, or fitness for a particular commercial purpose. Nothing in these terms limits rights or obligations that cannot lawfully be excluded. We may update these terms as tools, analytics, or advertising setups evolve, updating the effective date above accordingly.</p><p>For questions, see <a href="/contact/">Contact</a>. Read the <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="/editorial-policy/">Editorial Policy</a> for related information.</p></article>
